[[0,576520,0,7,1,6,"2015-10-10T00:57:50","Music_King","",[],"","A Russian Su-34 drops a guided KAB-500 bomb over Raqqa","http://www.gfycat.com/RemarkableShamefulChevrotain","MilitaryGifs"],[1,2774827,0,1,0,1,"2015-10-10T01:08:46","roznak","",[],"<p>And missed the giant building.</p>"],[1,2774893,0,0,0,0,"2015-10-10T01:15:07","gbj1301","",[],"<p>Were they aiming for the building?</p>"],[1,2775364,0,1,0,1,"2015-10-10T01:56:41","Beldin242","",[],"<p>It was only a warning shot.</p>"],[1,2779910,0,1,0,1,"2015-10-10T11:49:00","Longbow","",[],"<p>Since the building wasn't toasted, the target was probably designated by a ground observer or another aircraft and hit exactly what they wanted hit. That's much easier for the attacking aircraft since the pilot only needs to fly to the area and allow the weapon's sensor head to acquire the reflected designator. The pilot doesn't need to visually identify the precise target or even watch.</p>\n<p>The world has see so many US videos where the aircraft illuminates the target and also drops the bomb that they forget about ground observers or a spotter aircraft pointing the designator.</p>"]]
